{"kind":"assert","text":"CB-2 pre-source proposal. Published main contains AE-1 merge 3c8b8b8a and CB-1 source 8b1a3734. Use a production GitHub archive provider through the existing Room ArchiveDriver and archive target on celld. The owner configures the GitHub App installation that already authorizes the bound repository identity. Destination approval currently covers its exact repository and branch. Require explicit archive approval of the stable repository ID and exact journal refs. Check that binding again immediately before sending.\n\nThe owner configures the App key and any separate read credential in the private celld project. The provider mints repository-scoped installation credentials through the existing GitHub path, uses the expiry the provider returns and attempts revocation after the pass. Private read custody and the owners of rotation and reauthorization need the planner’s ruling.\n\nThe checked installed policy, recorded bind-archive, Directory target and archive driver select canonical journal objects, including the archive head and manifest, selected entries and approved retained replay material. Private native Register and Membership bodies stay under their existing archive rules. The provider supplies format, ref, objects, mintArchive, sendArchive and revokeArchive. It should implement readParent and readObject for the existing bounded adaptive path and preserve create-only or compare-and-swap ref writes. Unsupported bounded reads stop the pass.\n\nPlease decide the exact repository-to-journal-ref approval shape, private read credential ownership and lifetime, and whether the bounded adaptive path is mandatory for this first provider. The current GitHub fixture port contributes no production evidence."}